pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The positive half of the substitute-underflow pair, on the same shape the forgery uses: a
% database row whose degree is exactly `i64::MIN` and a witness that touches its variable, so
% the checker really does substitute into it. The proof is honest and must keep checking.
%
% It is the guard against a bogus fix. Refusing rows with extreme degrees, or clamping the
% substituted degree instead of escalating it, would pass every negative test in this defect's
% set and break this one.
f 2;
red 1 x3 >= 1 : x2 -> 1 x3 -> 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
